A/B: env-backed u-boot bootcount on openwrt-one (mt7981).

Adds BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT/ENV/ALTBOOTCMD to the spi-nand defconfig, after the
AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR line z01 adds. The counter is gated by the `upgrade_available`
env var, so steady-state boots neither count nor write the UBI env; once it
exceeds `bootlimit`, autoboot runs altbootcmd (A/B slot switch). Env persists in
the UBI ubootenv/ubootenv2 volumes (CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_UBI).

--- a/configs/mt7981_openwrt-one-spi-nand_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mt7981_openwrt-one-spi-nand_defconfig
@@ -19,3 +19,6 @@ CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_KEYED=y
 CONFIG_AUTOBOOT_STOP_STR=" "
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ENV=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD=y
 CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
